  "name": "Ball Lightning",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You create two globes of lightning that fly in whichever direction you indicate. For every 4 caster levels above 7th, you create an additional globe of lightning (3 globes at 11th, 4 globes at 15th, to the maximum of 5 globes at 19th). These globes fly at a rate of 20 feet per round and have perfect maneuverability. Wind does not affect a flying sphere’s course.\nIf a globe enters a space with a creature, it stops moving for the round and deals 3d6 points of lightning damage to that creature, though a successful Reflex save negates the damage. Creatures wearing metal armor take a -4 penalty on this Saving Throw.\nEach globe moves as long as you actively direct it (it’s a\nmove action\nfor you to direct all the spheres created by a single casting of this spell); otherwise they stay at rest. These globes have no mass and cannot push aside unwilling creatures or move solid objects. A ball lightning globe winks out if it exceeds the spell’s range.</p>",
      "instructions": "",
      "summary": "You create two globes of lightning that fly in whichever direction you indicate."
    },
